<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0e6c96ef-44a5-5b89-8cdf-c2e7dd44956d" activityNameId="c658d427-22ff-5722-8d53-f337b22f179c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cotton seed, at farm</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cotton seed, at farm
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg cotton fibre respectively cottonseed, both with a moisture content of 6%. Fresh matter yield at 6% moisture: 775 kg/ha cotton fibre and 1144 kg/ha cottonseed. The multioutput-process 'cotton, at farm' delivers the co-products 'cotton fibre, at farm' and 'cottonseed, at farm'. Economic allocation with allocation factor of 87.2% to fibre (exceptions see report).;
UUID: d2b9cebc-9633-3fd1-814b-763ec6da7197
The inventory includes the processes of soil cultivation, sowing, weed control, fertilisation, pest and pathogen control, irrigation, harvest and ginning. Machine infrastructure and a shed for machine sheltering is included. Inputs of fertilisers, pesticides and seed as well as their transports to the farm are considered. The direct emissions on the field are also included. The system boundary is at the farm gate. Raw cotton is separated into cotton fibres and cottonseed.
Location: Refers to an average production in the USA
Technology: Conventional production typical for the country. Water for irrigation is pumped from 48 meter depth by electric pumps.
Time period: The yield data have been collected for the years 2001-2006.
Production volume: US average prod of cotton 4'516'365t in 2001-2006. 
Sampling: Data come from the NREL database and from varoius U.S database. Data were compiled from statistics, literature, farm survey reports, documents from extension services, and expert knowledge. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d2b9cebc-9633-3fd1-814b-763ec6da7197.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
